From e2bc69584851d4808b9fb7f1038a1249bed4160b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 23:58:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(resource-packs): resolve licensed native image fallbacks

Bedrock 1.26.51.1 protocol 2193 accepts Hive item atlas aliases to vanilla images which the server does not resend. The bundled metadata archives intentionally contain no images, leaving these aliases unresolved during Java conversion.

Expose a platform provider for licensed image-only resource layers. Acquire them on the existing pack executor and wait alongside the server download without blocking its Netty event loop. Preserve native overlay precedence below bundled metadata and server packs, include their exact pixels in conversion cache fingerprints, and keep them outside server advertisements and pack identity tracking.

Native equipment can refer to built-in geometry, animations, controllers
and material parents. Permit these actor dependency documents from the
licensed provider while keeping them below server packs. Do not publish
unrelated block or entity definitions. Permit only the exact item and
terrain atlas paths needed for native icon selection. The synthetic shield
regression covers dependencies, server precedence and provenance.

Permit the exact native textures/item_texture.json and textures/terrain_texture.json atlases alongside licensed images. Its definitions are necessary to select built-in item sprites without server overrides.
